  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nPR #1304 leaves the fixed A8 simplex decoder on nonmatching P112 frame punctures open. This proves the sharp separate COPY cost **71** for the complementary **1,080 frames**, over arbitrary complex per-row kernel shifts. An all-nine-active exact witness attains the bound. The frame census partitions all 2,025 E8 eight-frames into the predecessor's 945 matching frames and these 1,080 frames, each consisting of one pair root and a Fano plane on the remaining coordinates.\n\nThis is a scoped proof with exhaustive finite lemmas, not a supplier or \u03ba improvement. The nine simplex normals are fixed, exactness is on all live pairs with ordinary transpose, and terms are billed separately. The COPY power bill also exceeds the eight rank-eight coordinate terms for `0<=a<1`, **when width, normalization and multiplicity are fixed**. No full supplier invoice is claimed. Only `research/a8-one-pair-frame-floor/` is added; no pending theorem is assumed for its bound.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- Task `complex-masked-decoder`, scope **refined** to PR #1304's explicit other-frame question; [task and overlap record](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/da6308454686c77372e82a60e196ccb828285360/research/a8-one-pair-frame-floor/TASK.json).\n- Research base: `ebedc0895eb4c06725af020bc1af165722b0a3ce` (priority revision 2); submission rebased onto `81e81af67714bdc8d1693b0bf5c29468b92f62ff`. Revision 3 was read and this completed COPY obstruction retained; it is not a new packing/\u03ba claim.\n- Contribution head: `da6308454686c77372e82a60e196ccb828285360`.\n- Predecessors: #1304 `a052f0da36a3845c2ec785fd44e5b9e50de3b688`; #1248 `f226f4329a996b0a1bea8794179a91b5d0ed80bf`; #1224 `00e6ed0810b8ebc7f6133e2c036d0f1c9a3a4162`. Their heads were rechecked. Source file blobs and hashes are pinned.\n- [Scoped claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1241#discussioncomment-18914233). Submission overlap covered 733 open PRs and 244 discussion records with complete pagination at 03:52 UTC on October 14. No competing result for this orbit was found within that coverage; no novelty guarantee.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/a8-one-pair-frame-floor\n```\n\nPassed on macOS arm64 / CPython 3.12.13. The primary checks all nine anchors: **390,915 binary planes, 20,019 partner-space tuples and 382,032 compatible choices**. Two sharp witnesses have costs `(0,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9)` and `(1,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9)`; both all-pairs identities are checked exactly. The [written proof](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/da6308454686c77372e82a60e196ccb828285360/research/a8-one-pair-frame-floor/PROOF.md) explains why the finite compatibility cover bounds every complex shift.\n\nThe second arithmetic implementation uses Gram-derived labels, nullspaces, Cartesian products and verified stabilizer transport. A separate pair/Fano construction agrees with the full frame census. Both implementations are explicitly credited adaptations of #1304; this is not independent peer review.\n\nTen semantic controls and all five package test groups pass, including false/missing/malformed receipts, incomplete anchor coverage, changed frame coverage, optimized execution and read-only relocation. Both mathematical checkers also pass under optimized CPython 3.14.6. The prescribed predecessor positive control, selected-result integrity check and metadata/source pins pass.\n\nNot checked: physical gathering, frames, restoration, hosting, precision/tape, all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source, analytic and bit H1\u2013H5 obligations. No selected cold replay, Lean, hosted-CI success, human review or maintainer acceptance is claimed.\n\n## Credit\n\ncommdata2338 (#1304) supplies the matching-frame result, both adapted implementations and the open question; Philipp/mightyOil (#1248) the deficiency method; joaqcoo (#1224) the normal form and A8 family. Credit the retained DreamingOfClouds (#717/#595/#446), Joel Pulikkan/GamingPuzzled (#620), themilkman216 (#968) and woklerx (#1077) lineage. Exact original file pins and adaptation notices are retained. Apache-2.0.\n\nPrepared for Hanson Sun (@bbMisk), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in the mathematics, implementations, verification and writing.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n[Structured questions and limits](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/da6308454686c77372e82a60e196ccb828285360/research/a8-one-pair-frame-floor/README.md#open-next-questions): a different specified nine-normal family, starting with its kernel-shift and column-rank calculation; or a physical shared-copy contract with a complete bill. The fixed simplex and separate-term assumptions block transferring this theorem to those cases.\n",
